{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T06:30:40.057038Z","id":"2c8723811217318104b825571db7e216bb56ba5986bcd3d6dfb4a2cfbce3f19b","body":{"detail":"Failure: body `.choose (.read 0) [(.present (.present .any), .literal (.boolean false)), (.any, .literal (.boolean true))]` (Rust `match x { Some(Some(_)) => false, _ => true }`) on input `.present (.present .unit)`: `pureValidate 10 body input = .ok false`, but `pureValidate 3 body input = .ok true` and `pureValidate 2 body input = .ok true`, both closed by `rfl` against the current State.lean. `pureMatch 0 _ _ _ = none` (line 2874) cannot be told apart from a pattern mismatch. `pureEval`'s `.choose` case (lines 2998-3003) uses `findSome?`, so a deep arm that runs out of fuel is skipped and a shallower wildcard arm runs instead. The generated validator `def <name> (fuel : Nat) (input : PureValue) := pureValidate fuel <name>_ir input` (provium/src/methods/validators.rs:1032) lets the consumer choose the fuel. A theorem or kernel-reduced native comparison at an insufficient fuel then certifies a result Rust never produces, with no `exhausted` fault. This contradicts the State.lean comment at lines 2823-2825 (\"Fuel exhaustion and malformed views are observable faults, never successful validations\") and provium/README.md lines 567-568 (\"Detected representation faults and exhaustion are explicit outcomes\").","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":2873},"end":{"line":2888},"content_hash":"72b3b61071b4ae64b83b7ba1b0fa8e6f8b042d432b9bd97f334e3f1d8c856bcf"},"suggested_fix":"Make pureMatch return a three-way result (for example `Except PureFault (Option PureEnv)`, or a dedicated inductive with matched/mismatched/exhausted). `.choose` should propagate exhaustion as `.error (.fault .exhausted)` instead of trying the next arm. Re-prove pure_match_* and pure_eval_step, and add a regression theorem showing that the example above at fuel 2 yields `.error .exhausted`.","summary":"pureMatch returns none on fuel exhaustion, so `choose` silently falls through to a later match arm instead of reporting `exhausted`","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T06:30:40.057215Z","id":"f4333daa416f40ea291e67034b23c1bc0d3c5d019c5bd22840b0cd145d1e6879","body":{"detail":"In pureMatch's `.variant` case, `fields.find? (fun field => field.1 == pair.1)` returning none makes the whole `foldlM` return none, which is the same as an ordinary pattern mismatch. In `pureEval`'s `.choose` (lines 2998-3003), the next arm, typically `_ => ...`, then runs and can return `.ok true`. A malformed `PureValue` (for example a variant missing a field that the Rust enum always has) therefore yields a successful validation through an arm Rust would never take. This contradicts the comment at State.lean:2823-2825 that malformed views are observable faults, never successful validations. README.md:566-568 says well-formed views are a separate premise, but it also says detected representation faults are explicit outcomes; here the defect is detectable and is dropped.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2881},"end":{"line":2887},"content_hash":"030b6ec78a5a0b29bc6de212aa495172c7d779d0e2baa966579ad382aa15e529"},"suggested_fix":"When the owner and tag match but a pattern field is missing from `fields`, return a representation fault rather than none (this needs the same three-way pureMatch result as the exhaustion fix). Then `.choose` reports `.fault .representation` instead of trying later arms.","summary":"A variant pattern over a view that lacks a named field fails to match and falls through to a later arm, instead of producing a representation fault","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T06:30:40.057336Z","id":"57ae76e0c83187632ad7709cc3195375aa8c2d522991e68b159999310404c863","body":{"detail":"`runSlotBatchPasses` evaluates `inputs[input]?.getD []` and `inputs[program.exclusionInput]?.getD []`. If the generated `passes` or `exclusionInput` names an index that does not exist (a frontend translation bug, or an input count that does not match the constructor's arguments), the pass inserts nothing and the exclusion check passes, and the batch can succeed. Only `required` is guarded, at line 598. The shared lemmas `runSlotBatch_valid`, `runSlotBatch_observes` and `runSlotBatch_accepts` (lines 712-867) are stated in terms of the same `getD []`. A consumer invariant proved over them therefore holds for a model that dropped a whole source slice. README.md:343-350 presents these as retaining nested enumeration and every pass, which a total extension hides.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":588},"end":{"line":599},"content_hash":"de21e489b8140a318fd62d28071bbeaf8478bd8e2e9caac3543ebbb69ec886c3"},"suggested_fix":"Return `.error` (a dedicated malformed-program code) when `inputs[input]?` or `inputs[program.exclusionInput]?` is none. Alternatively, add a well-formedness predicate (every pass index and the exclusion index are below `inputs.length`), have the generator emit a proof that it holds for each generated program, and require it as a premise of the shared lemmas.","summary":"Slot-batch passes read `inputs[i]?.getD []`, so an out-of-range input or exclusion index silently becomes an empty slice instead of a fault","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/FieldReads.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T06:30:40.057378Z","id":"f4f4b708bf31470fed9d59fa0247f34daa9f1b7e661840e5a218b46eaf45cc3e","body":{"detail":"`Loans.initial` (Loans.lean:78) gives every root stack ticket 0. `Live world reference` checks only `world reference.owner`, ticket equality, shared mode and the path prefix. If a World reassigns an owner after release (`release_valid` and then `acquire_valid`, Loans.lean:170-221, which only require `world owner = none`), a reference from the previous lifetime with ticket 0 becomes Live again over the new loan. `Arena.retired_not_revived` (Loans.lean:457-461) rules this out only for Arena-managed worlds. `ended_denied` (FieldReads.lean:169-171) states only that a removed owner denies access. README.md:227-233 claims that ending the loan invalidates subsequent dereferences, which holds only under the Arena discipline that these definitions do not mention.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":87},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"4f3a78443773faac24d16d2b7b863392ab22df4295e968c37e62e36cd2caf479"},"suggested_fix":"State Live and the dereference theorems over `Arena` (or include an allocation generation or root nonce in `Reference` and `Loan`). Add a theorem that a reference live before `Arena.endLifetime` is not live after any later `Arena.reserve`.","summary":"Borrowed reference liveness depends on Arena never reusing owner IDs, because every root ticket is 0, but Live and its theorems are stated over a bare World","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T06:30:40.057480Z","id":"ae6975bce568bbaba8804ea4ce77c8b69edeeda5d461b332b3adae8ab393784d","body":{"detail":"`selectRecord` builds the fallback with `initializeFields program.fallback (fun _ => 0)`. Any `.emptySlots (.parameter p)` field therefore gets length 0 instead of the instantiated const capacity. `initializeFields` (lines 1641-1643) also starts from `fun _ => .absent`, so a projection of a field the fallback omits reads as Rust `None` instead of failing. Current consumers (lookupRecord, recordAt, lastRecord, recovery) read only u64 leaves through `recordWord`, which rejects `.absent`, so no wrong result is known today. A future selector over a defaulted array or Option field would silently get the wrong value.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1733},"end":{"line":1736},"content_hash":"c338c029376ddfd9cc72bbb55a4eb823dd20e331163534bf759e3c084f101776"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the method's `sizes` into `selectRecord` (as `restoreState` already does for its constructor fields), and give InitCell an explicit `missing` cell (or return Option) for undeclared paths instead of defaulting to `.absent`.","summary":"selectRecord's fallback initializes capacity-parameter arrays with size 0 and reads undeclared paths as `.absent`","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T06:31:59.244413Z","id":"1d5837b9c11bd55382e88ead4f81803da36924e66e8af869bebc05df8a38eb8f","body":{"detail":"State.lean:2874 `| 0, _, _, _ => none` makes exhaustion indistinguishable from a mismatch; State.lean:2998-3003 `.choose` uses `arms.findSome?` over `pureMatch fuel`, so the next arm runs. Reproduced by copying State.lean lines 2823-3018 into a scratch file and running `elan run leanprover/lean4:v4.33.1 lean pure.lean` with body `.choose (.read 0) [(.present (.present .any), .literal (.boolean false)), (.any, .literal (.boolean true))]` on input `.present (.present .unit)`: `pureValidate 10` = `Except.ok false`, `pureValidate 3` = `Except.ok true`, `pureValidate 2` = `Except.ok true`; `example : pureValidate 3 ex inp = .ok true := by rfl` checks. The generated wrapper (provium/src/methods/validators.rs:1032) exposes fuel to the consumer. This contradicts the comment at State.lean:2823-2825. The blocker's Failure is concrete and reproduced.","kind":"comment","references":"2c8723811217318104b825571db7e216bb56ba5986bcd3d6dfb4a2cfbce3f19b","summary":"confirmed: fuel exhaustion in pureMatch falls through to a later choose arm and yields a successful, wrong validation","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T06:31:59.244451Z","id":"0a3faceec3bae9bc5c0c0670835222593090cb7326d3314d0cc3875776381440","body":{"detail":"State.lean:2884-2886: `let field <- fields.find? ...` inside `foldlM` in Option returns none for a missing field, which is the same as a mismatch. Reproduced in the same scratch copy of State.lean 2823-3018: `pureValidate 10 (.choose (.read 0) [(.variant \"E\" \"A\" [(\"x\", .any)], .literal (.boolean false)), (.any, .literal (.boolean true))]) (.variant \"E\" \"A\" [])` evaluates to `Except.ok true`, not a representation fault. Concern kind is appropriate because README.md:566-568 makes well-formed views a separate premise.","kind":"comment","references":"f4333daa416f40ea291e67034b23c1bc0d3c5d019c5bd22840b0cd145d1e6879","summary":"confirmed: a variant missing a pattern field is treated as a mismatch and a later arm returns ok","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T06:31:59.244461Z","id":"a250912896bfb07a8332b7423f373b38c65fb4a9ccc597579759bf88af43ec38","body":{"detail":"State.lean:592 `runSlotBatchPass program (inputs[program.exclusionInput]?.getD []) tag (inputs[input]?.getD []) [] entries`: a missing index means no insertions and no exclusions, and the result is still `.ok`. Only `required` is checked (State.lean:598), and that check also uses `getD []`. The generator (provium/src/methods/slot_batches.rs:607) emits the indices as raw numbers into `SlotBatch` and emits only an `rfl` correspondence theorem. Nothing proves the indices are in range. Concern kind is appropriate because no generated program is known to be malformed.","kind":"comment","references":"57ae76e0c83187632ad7709cc3195375aa8c2d522991e68b159999310404c863","summary":"confirmed: out-of-range pass and exclusion indices silently become empty slices","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/FieldReads.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T06:31:59.244471Z","id":"3da915486a0f52605d44f401594302df8cb48943da2fea0fd9650080086676f0","body":{"detail":"Loans.lean:50-52 `Stack.ticket (.root _) = 0` and Loans.lean:78 `initial` uses `.root frame`. FieldReads.lean:87-91 `Live` checks only `world reference.owner`, ticket equality, shared mode and path prefix. Loans.lean:168 `acquire_valid` requires only `world owner = none`, so a World can reacquire the same owner after `release_valid` (Loans.lean:213). Only `Arena.retired_not_revived` (Loans.lean:457-461) rules out reuse, and only for Arena. FieldReads.lean:169-171 `ended_denied` covers only the removed-owner state. The README.md:231 claim 'Ending the loan invalidates subsequent dereferences' therefore relies on the Arena discipline. Suggestion kind is appropriate.","kind":"comment","references":"f4f4b708bf31470fed9d59fa0247f34daa9f1b7e661840e5a218b46eaf45cc3e","summary":"confirmed: Live is stated over a bare World and every root ticket is 0, so owner reuse would revive old references","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T06:31:59.244482Z","id":"15ec6931b5858a50cdd915e69d5bcdfefd50e5682e8345af3610a32ff79f1d88","body":{"detail":"State.lean:1735 `| none => initializeFields program.fallback (fun _ => 0)`. With State.lean:1639-1640, `.emptySlots (.parameter p)` becomes `List.replicate 0 none`. State.lean:1641-1643 `initializeFields` folds from `fun _ => .absent`. The current callers (State.lean:1782, 1812, 1907, 1927, 2068, 2233, 2432) read u64 words, and `recordWord` (State.lean:2168-2171) maps `.absent` to none, so no wrong result is observable today. Suggestion kind is appropriate.","kind":"comment","references":"ae6975bce568bbaba8804ea4ce77c8b69edeeda5d461b332b3adae8ab393784d","summary":"confirmed: the selectRecord fallback uses size 0 for parameter capacities and reads undeclared paths as .absent","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.751819Z","id":"28e677884829489b0cea3bf4ba670931a65f28afabdd6f53493407c8af5fca3d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"pureMatch is now three-valued (Except PureFault (Option PureEnv)) and pureSelect propagates faults (provium/lean/Provium/State.lean). The theorem pure_choose_exhaustion_regression proves the reported example yields .error .exhausted at fuel 2 and 3 and .ok false at fuel 10; `cargo test --test validators -- --ignored` passed 6/6 with the new semantics.","supersedes":"2c8723811217318104b825571db7e216bb56ba5986bcd3d6dfb4a2cfbce3f19b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:19:17.751950Z","id":"f29e61f194a6f313fd15bce3a1199d34443f3055b39538dfded84a303883a95e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:105afefab66527086c063066e4b0a11d82ab24c1","summary":"A matching variant view that lacks a pattern field now returns .error .representation before any field is matched (pureMatch in provium/lean/Provium/State.lean). The theorem pure_choose_missing_field_regression proves the later wildcard arm no longer runs; validator Lean suite passed 6/6.","supersedes":"f4333daa416f40ea291e67034b23c1bc0d3c5d019c5bd22840b0cd145d1e6879","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T14:34:00.564949Z","id":"bcbdd34a644faf6629cde35319556d271a956613f246dda2051046aa20e6161f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:61c9cc8498e16c43df17d5b07779656f43c2c38e","summary":"Generated slot batches now prove `<method>_indices` (required, exclusion and every pass index below the argument count) by decide, audited with the generated theorems (provium/src/methods/slot_batches.rs, methods.rs). The total getD [] therefore never applies to generated programs. `cargo test --test slot_batches -- --ignored` passed and Jarl membership verified membership_Membership_restore_indices and membership_Membership_new_indices with no axioms. runSlotBatch itself is unchanged, preserving runSlotBatch_error_codes.","supersedes":"57ae76e0c83187632ad7709cc3195375aa8c2d522991e68b159999310404c863","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/State.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T14:34:00.565071Z","id":"15bde4ce057ca9c21da831b96361513ae526136d8f631a327657555c201f977c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:61c9cc8498e16c43df17d5b07779656f43c2c38e","summary":"lower_selection now rejects a fallback containing a capacity-parameter array, which selectRecord cannot instantiate (provium/src/methods/selectors.rs). Derived Default cannot build const-generic arrays, so no current source reaches it; the guard keeps any future fallback from silently getting length 0. Undeclared paths still read as .absent, which consumers reading u64 leaves through recordWord reject; `cargo test --test selectors -- --ignored` passed.","supersedes":"ae6975bce568bbaba8804ea4ce77c8b69edeeda5d461b332b3adae8ab393784d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/lean/Provium/FieldReads.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T14:34:00.565144Z","id":"8ef5a7757cb4595aa5c3f37fa5e17961eb39660bcafb01e88221a02ce0af927f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:61c9cc8498e16c43df17d5b07779656f43c2c38e","summary":"FieldReads.Borrowed.ended_not_revived proves that after Arena.endLifetime a reference into the ended loan is not Live, both immediately and after any later Arena.reserve, since owner IDs are never reused. It is audited in tests/borrowed_fields.rs (22 checks, passed); provium/README.md now states that liveness relies on this Arena discipline.","supersedes":"f4f4b708bf31470fed9d59fa0247f34daa9f1b7e661840e5a218b46eaf45cc3e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
